"""100 Australian clothing brands (C001-C100): the second cold email, rewritten after 0 real replies from the first
100 (26-27 Oct 2026: 3 bounces, 3 auto-replies, no answers yet, follow-ups not sent).

What changed from the first email, and why:
- It goes to a founder, press or marketing inbox where one is published, not customer care (Kivari's customer-care
  inbox turned the first email into a support ticket). Founders are greeted by name when the site names them.
- The ask is a ready-to-shoot 15-second ad script, free, "just reply yes", instead of a "2-minute teardown". A script
  is something they can use, and yes is one word.
- One specific idea built on a real product of theirs, under ~90 words, a plain subject about that product.
- Same rules as before: "At Mez Media, we scale brands", signed "Mez Media: we scale brands", no niche named in our
  own description, no results claimed, an opt-out line (Spam Act 2003: identify the sender, a working unsubscribe).

Every address was published on the brand's own site and its domain has a mail server (MX, checked 29 Oct 2026); see
leads/lead_database.csv for the page it came from and what each brand sells.
Usage: python3 outreach/clothing_au_emails.py  (prints every email; the drafts are made from TEMPLATE below)
"""

